#NEXUS

[ Gallina et al. 2014, PLOS ONE 9(5): e97128, Fig. 4: two slanted cladograms side by side, (A) strict consensus of the Diplodocoidea matrix with Leinkupal, 28 tips, and (B) a second analysis, 14 tips; open-circle nodes with clade names and support values in brackets. names.txt is for panel A (left). Panel A only (region box), 28 tips, slanted cladogram. The root node separates Shunosaurus from a polytomy of Omeisaurus, Losillasaurus, Jobaria, Camarasaurus, Haplocanthosaurus, (Australodocus, Brachiosaurus) and Diplodocoidea. Diplodocoidea = (Amphicoelias, (Rebbachisauridae, Flagellicaudata)): the second branch leaves the stem just after the Diplodocoidea circle. Diplodocidae is a 4-way node (Apatosaurus, Supersaurus, Dinheirosaurus, Diplodocinae). Topology transcribed from the figure and checked node by node against the image (2026-10-28); topology only, no support values or node numbers. Licence: CC BY. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=28;
    TAXLABELS
        Shunosaurus
        Omeisaurus
        Losillasaurus
        Jobaria
        Camarasaurus
        Haplocanthosaurus
        Australodocus
        Brachiosaurus
        Amphicoelias
        Amazonsaurus
        Histriasaurus
        Rebbachisaurus
        Zapalasaurus
        Limaysaurus
        Cathartesaura
        Demandasaurus
        Nigersaurus
        Suuwassea
        Amargasaurus
        Dicraeosaurus
        Brachytrachelopan
        Apatosaurus
        Supersaurus
        Dinheirosaurus
        Leinkupal
        Tornieria
        Diplodocus
        Barosaurus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE gallina2014a_fig4 = [&R] (Shunosaurus,(Omeisaurus,Losillasaurus,Jobaria,Camarasaurus,Haplocanthosaurus,(Australodocus,Brachiosaurus),(Amphicoelias,((Amazonsaurus,(Histriasaurus,Rebbachisaurus,Zapalasaurus,((Limaysaurus,Cathartesaura),(Demandasaurus,Nigersaurus)))),((Suuwassea,(Amargasaurus,(Dicraeosaurus,Brachytrachelopan))),(Apatosaurus,Supersaurus,Dinheirosaurus,(Leinkupal,(Tornieria,(Diplodocus,Barosaurus)))))))));
END;
